  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "All seven OnKill occurrences in the exact accepted Lua tree are one empty Skill default plus six localization-key strings. Each key exists in Weapons_ae.csv, Skill_OnKill labels the UI as 'On Kill:', no exact Lua function defines any key, and all six mechanics are implemented inside their weapon GetSkillEffect definitions.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "shipped_onkill_is_localized_metadata"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Luabind maps SkillEffect.iOwner to +0x5c. Board:AddEffect copies the 0x7c-byte record into its queue; both copy paths preserve +0x5c.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "skill_effect_owner_survives_queue"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The SkillEffect dispatcher passes the by-value record's +0x5c field into a context whose first field is owner, copies it, and conditionally installs it at current-context address 0x8bd254 before effect work.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "queued_owner_becomes_death_context"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Both Env_Attack ApplyEffect branches set effect.iOwner=ENV_EFFECT before Board:AddEffect, and exact native registration publishes ENV_EFFECT=-10.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "environment_effect_owner_is_minus_ten"
    },
    {
      "claim": "For non-Mech Pawn team 6 (TEAM_ENEMY), the death processor reads Minor at +0x10d0 and records event 2 with INT_MAX payload for non-Minor or event 12 for Minor. EVENT_ENEMY_KILLED is exactly event 2.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "ordinary_enemy_death_records_event_two"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The generic recorder increments pending event counts, the sole direct publisher copies pending to the readable array and resets pending, and registered Game:GetEventCount reads that array. Mission:BaseUpdate adds EVENT_ENEMY_KILLED to KilledVek for Kill Five and Pacifist objectives.",
      "classification": "inference",
      "id": "mission_kill_event_delivery"
    },
    {
      "claim": "For non-Minor, XP-eligible enemy deaths, owners 0..2 receive xp_<owner> and kill_<owner>; all other owners receive env_xp. Every reviewed enemy death also writes any_kill_<owner>.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "owner_specific_credit_split"
    },
    {
      "claim": "ENV_EFFECT owner -10 takes the outside-0..2 env_xp branch and names its unconditional bucket any_kill_-10. It therefore does not create the xp_<0..2>, kill_<0..2>, or any_kill_<0..2> entries consumed by those Mech owners, while the independent non-Minor mission event still fires.",
      "classification": "inference",
      "id": "environment_bypasses_mech_xp_and_kill_buckets"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The per-Pawn consumer reads and clears kill_<PawnID>, any_kill_<PawnID>, and xp_<PawnID>; applies Extra_XP as two per kill; routes XP into iKillCount +0xa60; and adds any-kill count to Mech iKills +0x98c.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "pawn_credit_consumer_and_named_fields"
    },
    {
      "claim": "iMissionDamage is bound at Pawn+0x1170 and updated by a separate health-delta accumulator. It is not the death-source owner or kill-credit path.",
      "classification": "fact",
      "id": "mission_damage_is_separate"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Rust apply_env_danger already records lethal enemy deaths through the shared mission-kill predicate, whose ordinary rule excludes Minor enemy units. No reviewed native rule contradicts the current simulator, so no semantic change or simulator-version bump follows.",
      "classification": "inference",
      "id": "rust_environment_kill_model_already_conforms"
    }
  ],
